--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. yasb -- vendored source code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

Files under vendor/win32/ are copied from yasb:

    https://github.com/amnweb/yasb
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024 amnweb
    Full licence text: vendor/LICENSE.yasb
    Imported at revision 95089f3cfffe5688911dc1a0e09dd959d49a321e

They are the Win32 plumbing layer -- ctypes bindings, structures, constants,
DWM backdrop, AppBar registration, global hotkeys, focus handling and icon
extraction.  The only modification applied is a mechanical rewrite of import
paths (core.utils.win32.* -> vendor.win32.*, core.events.service ->
vendor.compat.events).  vendor/win32/utils.py is a partial extract rather than
a full copy; the header on that file says so.

vendor/ is treated as read-only.  Behaviour changes belong in shell/platform/.

yasb's widget layer, settings UI, validation schemas and services were NOT
copied.  Where this project needed the same Windows API (media transport
controls, notification listening, audio endpoints, DDC/CI brightness, WLAN),
yasb's implementation was read as a reference and the code here was written
independently.

